    "summary": "Rare acoustic/electric set with stellar How Long Blues and New Speedway",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a tight acoustic half highlighted by How Long Blues and Deep Elem Blues, then flips into an electric surge featuring New Speedway Boogie, Cosmic Charlie and a fiery China Cat > I Know You Rider. Jerry’s tone is classic, the drummers are “smoking,” and the recording captures the energy despite a few tape cuts.",
    "review": "On July 14, 1970 at San Rafael's Euphoria Ballroom the Dead gave fans a unique blend of acoustic intimacy and electric firepower. The first set rolls through folk‑rock staples – Don’t Ease Me In, Friend Of The Devil and Dire Wolf – before settling into a bluesy showcase with How Long Blues (Jerry’s solo shines) and Deep Elem Blues. The second half erupts with New Speedway Boogie, a raw China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue, and the thunderous drumming that drives Cosmic Charlie and Good Lovin'. Despite occasional tape glitches on Easy Wind and an early cut of Good Lovin', the soundboard capture is crisp enough to hear Pigpen’s organ texture and Phil’s high‑in‑the‑mix solo. The encore rounds it out with a heartfelt Uncle John’s Band, making this one of the most compelling snapshots of the 1970 lineup.",
